index e625c35..6d7fdd7 100644
--- a/docs/buzz-help.md
+++ b/docs/buzz-help.md
@@ -4,6 +4,33 @@ Use this guide when helping someone use Buzz. Explain in their terms, not
 implementation details. This is an overview, not a complete feature list. Use
 current app context and available tools to check anything it does not cover.
 
+## Team Web deployment
+
+In the Team Web build, sign in with the invited team account and password. The
+server holds and signs with the Buzz identity; a browser does not receive the
+private key. Team settings are available at `/?team-settings` for invitations,
+model configuration and sign-out. These account flows replace desktop identity
+setup in this build.
+
+In a connected group, explicitly @ the group assistant to submit remote work.
+Closing the browser does not stop it. The **群任务** button in the chat header
+shows persisted task states; select a task to open its existing Buzz thread, or
+use Stop to request cancellation. Generated files are retained after cancellation.
+“需要核对” is an unresolved state, not completion; “正在停止” is a request awaiting
+confirmation from the runtime. A connection error leaves the last known state
+visible and does not imply that work completed.
+
+The right pane is the native Harness workspace. Open **Workspace files** to
+view generated files. Group members share the files and execution session while
+keeping their own open tabs. Replies open in the center conversation pane;
+Harness remains visible on the right. Close the reply tab or select the chat tab
+to return to the conversation. Personal and group spaces are isolated, and
+removed members lose workspace access. Current Team Web supports explicit @ work;
+proactive group listening and expert handoffs are not yet exposed. The Add menu
+creates a group or Agent; Contacts opens people and Agents for direct messaging.
+Do not suggest desktop runtime installation or a shared cloud desktop as a Team
+Web capability.
+
 ## Start with useful work
 
 Buzz is an open-source app for thinking, asking questions, and getting work done
@@ -327,3 +354,78 @@ Release builds ignore this optional helper.
 ### Builderlab in development
 
 With the pinned-viewer development server, Settings → Plugins → Builderlab manages one sign-in for hosted communities, remote agents and apps. It survives app reloads while the server runs. Signing out or session expiry signs all three out. The credential stays on the server and is not saved to disk.
+
+### Team Web IM
+
+The LAN Web build opens directly into conversations. Search and Add are above
+recent chats; the account avatar and Contacts are at the bottom-left. There is
+no global platform header or desktop Agent management page.
+
+Add offers only Create group chat and Create Agent. A group can include coworkers
+and Agents. An Agent has a name and role instructions; creating one opens its
+private conversation. Contacts lists coworkers and available server Agents and
+opens real direct messages. Server registration is confirmed before an Agent is
+shown as ready. New workspaces may take a moment to start on the server.
+
+Agent creation includes four character shapes and six color palettes. The selected
+portrait follows that identity into chats and Contacts. Group portraits combine
+actual members, including Agents. While work runs, the conversation header shows
+each active Agent once, with motion that respects reduced-motion preferences.
+
+Private Agent messages do not require @. Groups use explicit @ mentions. New final
+results appear in their original discussion and in the chat. Supported `/work/`
+file buttons open the original Harness preview. Private workspaces are owned by
+their user; group workspaces have separate runtimes and files. Different Agents
+have distinct native sessions. These Web identities are server-managed and do not
+use Buzz's desktop Agent library.
+
+Adding an available server Agent through the native group membership flow also
+prepares its group execution session. Only an authorized group administrator can
+add an Agent they own (or the shared coordinator). Requests queue while the
+workspace starts. An @ alone does not add an Agent to a group. Group requests can
+use a bounded selection of recent group messages; they do not load private chats.
+
+While a task runs, its request shows the real streaming response, current stage
+and expandable tool inputs/results. The progress view keeps a bounded excerpt;
+it does not expose private reasoning or replace the native Harness workspace.
+The formal chat result takes over the text after delivery. A connection warning
+keeps the last observed state and does not mean work stopped. Stop requests use
+the existing task cancellation. Completed ordinary replies with no process notes
+do not keep an empty progress row.
+
+The native Harness sidebar includes a **工作直播** tab. Everyone with current
+conversation access sees the same public task progress, growing response and tool
+records. Active tasks expand; completed work collapses. File previews remain native,
+and updates do not change another member's selected tab. Team Web interface copy
+and the embedded native workspace open in Chinese; names, messages and file contents
+are preserved. The activity feed removes tasks that leave its bounded window so a
+finished task cannot remain falsely marked as running.
+
+The character blinks at rest and breathes while the task ledger reports work.
+Motion pauses in hidden tabs and respects Reduced Motion. Task status text remains
+authoritative. Native Harness tabs and tools keep their original UI.
+
+Team Web now has a narrow left rail: switch between chats and the inline contacts
+list without changing the open conversation or its draft. Click a contact to open
+a chat. Your profile stays at the bottom; the bell opens Notifications. Unread
+marks remain red even on a selected row, with the existing mute/read policy.
+Allow browser notifications there for running-tab alerts, choose per-category
+sounds, use **试听** to preview, or turn sound off. Browser/system permission and
+audio policy still apply. Message portraits align with the start of each author's
+message group, while focused portraits remain mounted during live updates.
+
+The native Harness **开始** page exposes workspace files, a user terminal and a
+browser. New workspace bindings keep that guide instead of forcing the live tab.
+An Agent can use `open_browser` to publish a page to the conversation workspace;
+new successful requests open native browser tabs for members following the guide,
+live view or browser. Other selected files/terminals stay selected. Historical
+requests open only on explicit action. This tool does not read pages or perform
+browser clicks, forms or login. Web embedding still follows the site's iframe
+policy. Native terminal commands are entered by people; automatic Agent shell
+authorization is not enabled by this integration.
+
+Team Web can be installed from Chrome as **群体智能**, opening in its own window.
+Use **安装应用** at the bottom of the left rail or Chrome's address-bar install
+action. Installation needs a trusted HTTPS connection and a normal browser window.
+The installed window uses the same account and remote services. Offline navigation
+shows a reconnect page; messages, files and authenticated responses are not cached.
